# `dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer`

Minimises a black box with mesh adaptive direct search, with constraints, several objectives, failed evaluations, a cache and a surrogate.

## Signature

```cpp
dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer(const std::function<dfo::BlackboxEvaluation(const pluss::Series &)> &blackbox, const pluss::Series &initial, const dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig &config = {});
template <class Fn> dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer(Fn &&blackbox, const pluss::Series &initial, const dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig &config = {});
```

## What It Does

The general mesh-adaptive solver and the one the front door runs for a black box. The callback returns a [`BlackboxEvaluation`](BlackboxEvaluation.md): one or more **objectives**, optional **constraints** (`g(x) ≤ 0`), a flag for a **failed** evaluation and a flag for whether the call **counts**. Constraints are handled by the policy in [`ConstraintHandling`](ConstraintHandling.md); several objectives are reduced to one by a [scalarisation](MultiObjectiveScalarization.md) while the non-dominated points are kept in an archive; evaluated points are cached, and an optional [surrogate](SurrogateMode.md) orders the poll candidates so that an opportunistic poll stops sooner. The poll scheme follows the configuration, orthogonal by default.

## Parameters

`Fn &&blackbox`
: A callable returning a `BlackboxEvaluation`, a `Series` of objectives or a number.

`const pluss::Series &initial`
: The starting point.

`const dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig &config`
: The settings.

## Returns

A [`BlackboxAdvancedOutcome`](BlackboxAdvancedOutcome.md).

## Errors

- A black box that returns neither objectives nor a failure flag throws on the first call.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A black box with an objective only.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto black_box = [](const Series &x) {
    dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
    e.objectives = (x - 3.0).square().sum().reshape({1});   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)
    return e;
  };

  const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome o = dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer(black_box, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}));
  out.writeln("minimizer =", o.minimizer.items<double>(), ", minimum =", o.scalarized_minimum, ", status =", dfo::to_string(o.status));
}
```

### Example 2

Failed evaluations. The simulator fails where `x₀ > 1.5`, so the best usable point is at the edge of the failing region, `(1.5, 1)`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(3));
  std::int64_t failures = 0;
  const auto black_box = [&](const Series &x) {
    dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
    if (x.select(0, 0).item<double>() > 1.5) {
      ++failures;
      e.evaluation_ok = false;
      e.objectives = pluss::make_series(0.0).reshape({1});
      return e;
    }
    e.objectives = (x - pluss::series::make({2.0, 1.0})).square().sum().reshape({1});
    return e;
  };
  const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome o = dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer(black_box, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}));
  out.writeln("minimizer =", o.minimizer.items<double>(), ", minimum =", o.scalarized_minimum, ", failed calls =", failures);
}
```

### Example 3

Two objectives with a Chebyshev scalarisation. For `f₁ = x`, `f₂ = 1 − x²` on `[0, 1]` (a non-convex front) the compromise `x = 0.618` balances the two.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto black_box = [](const Series &x) {
    dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0);
    e.objectives = a.reshape({1}).unite({(1.0 - a.square()).reshape({1})}, 0);
    return e;
  };
  dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig config;
  config.lower_bounds = pluss::series::make({0.0});
  config.upper_bounds = pluss::series::make({1.0});
  config.multiobjective_scalarization = dfo::MultiObjectiveScalarization::Chebyshev;
  config.objective_weights = pluss::series::make({1.0, 1.0});
  config.objective_reference = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  config.max_evaluations = 3000;
  const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome o = dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer(black_box, pluss::series::make({0.8}), config);
  out.writeln("x =", o.minimizer.items<double>(), ", objectives =", o.objective_vector.items<double>());
}
```

